    "created_at": "2017-05-23T10:01:51Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-05-23T10:01:51Z",
    "body": "> If we want to do this, we should pull back hierarchy restriction first.\r\n\r\nThat's https://github.com/whatwg/fullscreen/pull/91, but does it need to block this change? I think that with or without hierarchy restrictions, fullscreenchange events can bubble through elements that both are and are not in top layer, so one has to look at the event target. I'm in no hurry to get rid of the hierarchy restrictions in Blink, but would it be unworkable to not have them? (As you can tell, I'm conflicted.)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/fullscreen/issues/comments/303351694/reactions",
